    "description": "Restructured ALU computation from serial (opcode->alu_op case->ALU op->result) to parallel (compute ADD and SUB unconditionally in wires, late 2:1 mux select using pre-decoded opcode one-hot signals). Eliminates serial opcode->alu_op->ALU dependency from critical path feeding st_0000's PC and ALU_OUT register updates. Added one-hot pre-decode of opcode (op_is_add, op_is_addi, op_is_sub, op_is_cmp) and ALU group signals (alu_op_is_add, alu_op_is_sub) to reduce opcode fanout and drive mux select. Expected WNS +5-15%, TNS +10-20%.",
    "anti_pattern_avoided": "condition_precompute on PC (cpu_fsm v0.1 anti-pattern) - used late_mux_select instead which preserves all assignment semantics"
  },
